# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal and working documents, not published (D038)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D038 untracked nine documents. D039 reversed that for eight of them: the
# findings they were meant to protect were already public, so withholding
# REPORT.md removed the study's only statement of its own limits while leaving
# every number it qualifies, and LICENSE/LICENSE-docs/CITATION.cff all cited a
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md that was not shipped.
#
# HANDOVER.md stays withheld: it is the one of the nine with no scientific
# content and the only one a publication-safety scan flagged -- it records the
# project's cloud spend and a credential-scope instruction. It remains on disk
# and in this repository's history; untracking removes it from the published
# tree, not from a clone (D038 section 2).
HANDOVER.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Withheld on public release (D037)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The T-A4 experiment proposal is an internal document that was "not yet
# preregistered or executed" when written. Its content is withheld; its title,
# size and SHA-256 are committed in the stub beside it, so every reference to
# it elsewhere still resolves to something a reader can verify.
PXD024871_CNN_Experiment_Proposal.md
!PXD024871_CNN_Experiment_Proposal.STUB.md

# Verbatim stdout of NetMHCpan 4.1 and MixMHCpred 3.0 (37 MB). The per-peptide
# SCORE CSVs are committed -- they are the evidence behind the four-predictor
# comparison in §18 and are ordinary derived results. The raw program output is
# not committed, because both tools reach users through an academic licence and
# republishing their verbatim output is the part of this that comes closest to
# redistributing the tools themselves. The files are kept on local disk: they
# exist so that a parsing error never costs a 45-minute re-score again, which
# is exactly what it cost once (see the header of predict_netmhcpan.py).
results/predictors/netmhcpan_raw/
results/predictors/mixmhcpred_raw/

# Superseded duplicates, byte-identical to the five-predictor-era names that
# replaced them. Hashes recorded in D037; nothing was deleted from disk.
data/derived/TEST_PREDICTOR_OVERLAP_2_0_0.csv
data/derived/TEST_PREDICTOR_OVERLAP_2_3_0.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party data and models obtained under their own licences
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw PAYLOADS are not committed: the containers are tens of gigabytes and the
# repository is not their archive. Provenance records are committed, because
# they are what make absent payloads verifiable.
#
# The small authoritative inputs ARE committed. The manifest and the metadata
# file total under a megabyte, every pipeline stage reads them, and excluding
# them made the repository non-self-contained: a fresh clone could not run
# batch_extract.py at all, which is how this was found.
#
# S5 and S6 additionally MAY NOT be redistributed: the UniProt human proteome,
# the MHCflurry training corpora, the NetMHCpan 4.2 training set and the
# MixMHCpred training table each carry their own terms. DATA_SOURCES.md records
# where each came from and its SHA-256, which is what reproducibility needs.
data/raw/**
!data/raw/
!data/raw/*/
!data/raw/*/provenance.jsonl
!data/raw/S1/*.json
!data/raw/S2/*.tsv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PXD004023, the external replication cohort (D054)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retrieved payloads are not committed, by the same rule that applies to S3 and
# S4: the identification containers are 1.1 GB and the acquisition-file headers
# 161 MB, against a tracked payload of 110 MB. Provenance IS committed --
# header_checksums.txt and the two manifests -- which is what makes an absent
# payload verifiable. scripts/fetch_px4023.sh retrieves both on demand.
data/external/PXD004023/mzid/
data/external/PXD004023/hdr/

# units.json holds derived peptide sequences from the deposit. It is withheld
# pending the redistribution position for PXD004023, which is not established
# (D054 section 4). It is declared absent in scripts/check_references.py, so the
# reference gate reports it rather than passing silently. Lifting this line is
# the whole of the change if the terms permit redistribution.
data/external/PXD004023/units.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient stdout/stderr capture from runs. The provenance artifacts are the
# CSV and params JSON a run writes, not its progress stream.
results/**/run.log
results/**/run.err

# Agent/editor session state, not project content.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

